eta.env.VITE_BACKEND_URL`. We can set in dev using .env. But simpler for now: host 'http://localhost:3000'. Provide.\n\nLet's create client/.env with VITE_BACKEND_URL= http://localhost:3000. And main.js uses import.meta.env.VITE_BACKEND_URL.\n\nAdd client/.env file.\n\nAlso add client/vite.config.js to set base path? default is '/', ok.\n\nImplement.\n\nAlso ensure that the package.json has dev scripts referencing client correctly.\n\nLet's create these files.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"write_file","arguments":"{\"path\":\"client/index.html\",\"content\":\"<!DOCTYPE html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n  <meta charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\" />\\n  <title>Realtime Board</title>\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n  <h1>Realtime Board</h1>\\n  <div id=\\\"messages\\\" style=\\\"border:1px solid #ccc; padding:10px; height:300px; overflow-y:scroll;\\\"></div>\\n  <form id=\\\"form\\\" style=\\\"margin-top:10px;\\\">\\n    <input type=\\\"text\\\" id=\\\"input\\\" autocomplete=\\\"off\\\" placeholder=\\\"Type a message\\\" required />\\n    <button type=\\\"submit\\\">Send</button>\\n  </form>\\n  <script type=\\\"module\\\" src=\\\"/src/main.js\\\"></script>\\n</body>\\n</html>\\n\"}"}}]}
