0.40.723.301 D Parsed message: {"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We've created server.js and rewrite db.run to get. But `db.get` returns only first row; good.\n\nNeed to set up client src main.js. Also create vite config to serve static index? The client will run on default Vite dev server at port 5173. But backend server may run on 3000. To connect cross-origin, we need CORS. Already server has cors. Good.\n\nIn client, import from server endpoints: GET /api/messages, POST, SSE.\n\nImplement main.js with fetch, EventSource, DOM update.\n\nAlso we need to ensure NPM script \"dev:frontend\" works: It runs npm run dev --prefix client. But we need repository structure: root, client subfolder. We have client folder created. In root we have package.json referencing concurrent. Need to create client src directory and main.js.\n\nAlso need to set Vite config? We don't need complex config. By default Vite serves index.html from root or from the folder. In the client folder, index.html is at root, but script src \"/src/main.js\" will need src folder. We'll create client/src/main.js.\n\nLet's create that file and implement logic.\n\nAlso for the show of messages we need to create a function to render message list. We may push a new message to the end.\n\nEdge: In SSE event, the data: lines send JSON, we parse via event.data. Use onmessage event.\n\nImplementation:\n\nconst baseUrl = 'http://localhost:3000'; or process.env? But we can get from window location. Since dev servers run on different ports, we won't have a proxy. So we can use: const baseUrl = 'http://localhost:3000'; In production would need same origin, but okay.\n\nImplement fetchMessages: GET baseUrl + '/api/messages'; then fill messages container.\n\nImplement sendMessage: fetch POST with JSON.\n\nImplement EventSource: new EventSource(baseUrl + '/api/stream'); onmessage: parse JSON, call append.\n\nAlso form submission handler: preventDefault, call sendMessage. Clear input if succeed.\n\nTesting wise: When we submit a POST, the server inserts and broadcast; SSE receives.\n\nAlso we need to ensure front-end knows to circumvent CORS? Already configured.\n\nAlso need to expose root path for static assets. Vite dev server might not host built assets for server because server may serve static files from client? Actually the backend server just serves API. In dev mode, frontend is served by Vite dev server, not backend. That means the page is not served by backend. The backend just API + SSE. To load the page initially, we could open http://localhost:5173/ which is Vite dev. That works. But dev instructions said npm run dev start both backend and frontend. That will open Vite dev server. The page will load and connect to API port 3000. That should be fine.\n\nDo we need to add output with ts? no.\n\nAlso need to set \"type\":\"module\" to import? main.js will use ES modules simply.\n\nLet's add main.js content.\n\nAlso ensure we have \"public\" folder? Not needed.\n\nLet's create client/src/main.js.\n\nLet's proceed.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"write_file","arguments":"{\"path\":\"client/src/main.js\",\"content\":\"// Simple front-end logic for the realtime board\\nconst BASE_URL = 'http://localhost:3000';\\nconst messagesEl = document.getElementById('messages');\\nconst inputEl = document.getElementById('input');\\nconst formEl = document.getElementById('form');\\n\\n// Utility to append a message element\\nfunction appendMessage(msg) {\\n  const div = document.createElement('div');\\n  div.textContent = `[${new Date(msg.created_at).toLocaleTimeString()}] ${msg.text}`;\\n  messagesEl.appendChild(div);\\n  messagesEl.scrollTop = messagesEl.scrollHeight;\\n}\\n\\n// Load history\\nasync function loadHistory() {\\n  try {\\n    const res = await fetch(`${BASE_URL}/api/messages`);\\n    const data = await res.json();\\n    data.forEach(appendMessage);\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    console.error('Failed to load history', err);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// Submit new message\\nasync function postMessage(text) {\\n  const res = await fetch(`${BASE_URL}/api/messages`, {\\n    method: 'POST',\\n    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\\n    body: JSON.stringify({ text }),\\n  });\\n  const data = await res.json();\\n  if (!res.ok) {\\n    alert('Error: ' + (data.error || 'Unknown'));\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  // message will arrive via SSE as well; we can rely on that\\n}\\n\\n// SSE listener\\nfunction initSSE() {\\n  const es = new EventSource(`${BASE_URL}/api/stream`);\\n  es.onmessage = (e) => {\\n    try {\\n      const msg = JSON.parse(e.data);\\n      appendMessage(msg);\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      console.error('Failed to parse SSE data', err);\\n    }\\n  };\\n  es.onerror = (err) => {\\n    console.error('SSE error', err);\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nformEl.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {\\n  e.preventDefault();\\n  const text = inputEl.value.trim();\\n  if (!text) return;\\n  postMessage(text);\\n  inputEl.value = '';\\n});\\n\\n// Initialisation\\nloadHistory();\\ninitSSE();\\n\"}"}}]}
